specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:331:5. If the tool returned `clientMessages`, they are forwarded to the frontend as-is, in one `tool_result` chunk ([validated by: forwards the client messages a tool returned as one tool_result chunk](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L494))
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:332:6. If the tool set `suppressAssistantResponse`, the AI's next reply is kept in session context but hidden from the frontend ([validated by: asks for suppression when the tool says the reply is already handled](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L525))
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:333:7. The orchestrator re-queries the AI provider with the updated messages, and the chunks of every round reach the client in order ([validated by: runs another round after a tool call and streams both rounds in order](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L459))
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:334:8. This repeats while `round <= maxToolRounds`, counted from zero, so the default of 5 permits six model calls in total ([validated by: stops asking for tools once maxToolRounds is spent](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L480))
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:345:- The loop ends as soon as a round stops with `end_turn`, and nothing further is asked of the provider ([validated by: stops after one round when nothing asked for a tool](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L471)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:346:- An `entry_upsert` a tool returns is appended to the session and its index rewritten to the position it actually landed in, because a tool cannot know how long the session already is ([validated by: appends an upserted entry to the session and rewrites its index to match](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L508)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:347:- The response text a hook sees is the text of every round joined, not only the last ([validated by: joins the text of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L537)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:348:- Usage an earlier round reported is kept when a later round reports none, so a tool round does not erase the token count ([validated by: keeps the usage an earlier round reported when a later round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L559)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-responses/spec.md:117:2. `suppressAssistantResponse: true` hides the AI's follow-up. The AI still receives the result string (so it has context for follow-ups), but the client does not see the AI echoing "100 miles equals 160.93 km." ([validated by: asks for suppression when the tool says the reply is already handled](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L525)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-responses/spec.md:153:Tools do not have access to the session, so they cannot know the correct entry index. The orchestrator handles this automatically: any `entry_upsert` message in `clientMessages` gets its `index` replaced with the real value by appending the entry to the session. The tool can set `index` to any value -- it will be overwritten ([validated by: appends an upserted entry to the session and rewrites its index to match](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L508)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:12:- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a required-property rejection without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:13:- A nested missing property is reported with its complete JSON Pointer path, including the containing object ([validated by: names the nested required property in a schema rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L33)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:14:- A nested wrong-typed property is reported with its complete JSON Pointer path and expected type ([validated by: names the nested property path for a type rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L82)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:15:- An enum rejection is reported with the failing property's JSON Pointer path ([validated by: names the property path when an enum constraint rejects input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L108)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:16:- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: names the top-level property and expected type for a type rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L60), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:17:- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input and undeclared properties through unchanged once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L130)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:19:- An unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: throws for an unregistered tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L222)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:24:- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses a static validator after the schema object changes](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L153)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:25:- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L180)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:30:- A rejected tool call is visible to the provider as a `tool_result`, and a corrected retry can execute and complete the message without rejecting `processMessage` ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back for a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L403)).
